  "rationale": "This inscription is a classic Athenian treasury inventory from the Parthenon, dated to 413/2 BC (IG I³ 302). It records the formal transfer of sacred objects (anathemata) from the outgoing board of Treasurers of Athena to the incoming board. The text lists a variety of precious items, including golden crowns, silver bowls (phialai), furniture (thrones and couches), and musical instruments (lyres), often specifying their weight in drachmas. The presence of demotics (Acharnae, Aphidna, Phrearrhioi, Eupyridai, Paiania) and the mention of the Parthenon confirm its Athenian origin and administrative function.",
